From a16003602fec28637366c0315c7eead9dec453ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:28:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] resource-network: free a rig after use

- POST /v1/bookings/{id}/release: the contractor who booked it or the rig's owner ends an accepted booking (status completed) and the rig is available again. Idempotent; 403 for anyone else; 409 for a booking that was never accepted.
- an owner setting a rig back to available now also ends its accepted booking. Before, the booking kept blocking every new request with RESOURCE_ALREADY_REQUESTED even though the rig showed available.
- job.completed subscriber (app/job_consumer.py, same shape as platform-spine's payment consumer) frees the rigs booked for a job automatically. Redis pub/sub is lossy, so the manual release stays as the fallback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BHz41VwRigfURYpC97T6Az
